        "original_id": "1a4ba8ad-e3af-5f54-908e-b565447f971d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric Maskin, Leonid Hurwicz, Roger Myerson, Abraham Flexner, Louis Bamberger, Caroline Bamberger Fuld, Peter Sarnak\n- Organizations: Harvard University, Institute for Advanced Study, School of Mathematics\n- Places: Princeton, New Jersey, United States\n- Roles: Adams University Professor, permanent faculty\n- Concepts: mechanism design theory\n- Topics: economics, theoretical research, intellectual inquiry\n\nFacts:\n- The Institute for Advanced Study is an independent postdoctoral research center for theoretical research and intellectual inquiry in Princeton, New Jersey, United States.\n- The Institute for Advanced Study was founded in 1930 by Abraham Flexner together with Louis Bamberger and Caroline Bamberger Fuld.\n- Eric Stark Maskin was born on December 12, 1950.\n- Eric Maskin is an American economist.\n- Eric Maskin shared the 2007 Nobel Prize with Leonid Hurwicz and Roger Myerson for laying the foundations of mechanism design theory.\n- Eric Maskin is the Adams University Professor at Harvard University.\n- Peter Sarnak is on the permanent faculty of the School of Mathematics at the Institute for Advanced Study.",
